From: Anaconda recipe maintenance <pkg-team@anaconda.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Increase autograd python_functions codegen sharding 5 -> 10

A single generated python_functions_N.cpp shard costs ~14GB to compile with
MSVC targeting arm64, exceeding the 16GB PBP win-arm64 worker's memory
watchdog even with fully serialized compiles (pytorch-feedstock#118). Halving
the per-shard content brings each TU to ~7GB, which fits.

TWO edits are required and must stay in sync:
  1. tools/autograd/gen_autograd_functions.py: num_shards drives BOTH the
     python_functions.h forward-declares/init-calls and the .cpp writer.
  2. caffe2/CMakeLists.txt: GENERATED_CXX_PYTHON hardcodes the shard file
     list the build actually compiles. Without extending it, codegen emits
     10 balanced shards but CMake compiles only 0..4 — dropping half the
     autograd function registrations (a silent-miscompile, not just a
     no-op). The generator count and this list MUST match.

The python_torch_functions_* count is deliberately left at 3 — it must stay
synced with gatherTorchFunctions in python_torch_functions_manual.cpp and is
not the memory hotspot.

Applied only on win-arm64 via a meta.yaml patch selector.
---
 caffe2/CMakeLists.txt                    | 5 +++++
 tools/autograd/gen_autograd_functions.py | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/caffe2/CMakeLists.txt b/caffe2/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/caffe2/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/caffe2/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -292,6 +292,11 @@ set(GENERATED_CXX_PYTHON
   "${TORCH_SRC_DIR}/csrc/autograd/generated/python_functions_2.cpp"
   "${TORCH_SRC_DIR}/csrc/autograd/generated/python_functions_3.cpp"
   "${TORCH_SRC_DIR}/csrc/autograd/generated/python_functions_4.cpp"
+  "${TORCH_SRC_DIR}/csrc/autograd/generated/python_functions_5.cpp"
+  "${TORCH_SRC_DIR}/csrc/autograd/generated/python_functions_6.cpp"
+  "${TORCH_SRC_DIR}/csrc/autograd/generated/python_functions_7.cpp"
+  "${TORCH_SRC_DIR}/csrc/autograd/generated/python_functions_8.cpp"
+  "${TORCH_SRC_DIR}/csrc/autograd/generated/python_functions_9.cpp"
   "${TORCH_SRC_DIR}/csrc/autograd/generated/python_variable_methods.cpp"
   "${TORCH_SRC_DIR}/csrc/autograd/generated/python_torch_functions_0.cpp"
   "${TORCH_SRC_DIR}/csrc/autograd/generated/python_torch_functions_1.cpp"
diff --git a/tools/autograd/gen_autograd_functions.py b/tools/autograd/gen_autograd_functions.py
--- a/tools/autograd/gen_autograd_functions.py
+++ b/tools/autograd/gen_autograd_functions.py
@@ -568,7 +568,7 @@ def gen_autograd_functions_python(
     template_path: str,
 ) -> None:
     fm = FileManager(install_dir=out, template_dir=template_path, dry_run=False)
-    num_shards = 5
+    num_shards = 10
     fm.write(
         "python_functions.h",
         lambda: {
